  "definition": "Design Requirements for Residential, Commercial, and Industrial Development Projects",
  "effectiveDate": "2020-10-23",
  "historyNote": "#12805, eff 12-15-19; ss by #12954, eff 12-24-19; amd by #13124, eff 10-23-20",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-Wt 524.04",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 524.04 Design Requirements for Residential, Commercial, and Industrial Development Projects",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 524.04 Design Requirements for Residential, Commercial, and Industrial Development Projects. In addition to meeting the applicable design requirements established in Env-Wt 300, a residential, commercial, or industrial development project in non-tidal wetlands shall be designed to meet the following criteria:\n\n(a) The project complies with all applicable requirements of Env-Wt 400, Env-Wt 700, Env-Wt 800, Env-Wt 900, and other applicable project-specific criteria in this chapter;\n\n(b) The project does not use wetlands or surface waters to serve as stormwater or water quality treatment;\n\n(c) The project provides setbacks and water quality protection measures sufficient to protect private and public drinking water supplies, source water protection areas, and fisheries;\n\n(d) The project maintains or restores hydrologic connections to maintain flows necessary to preserve adjacent wetland and riparian functions;\n\n(e) The project maintains existing fishery spawning, feeding, or cover habitat and fish passage necessary to maintain fishery or habitat or populations; and\n\n(f) The project maintains existing wetland-dependent wildlife habitat and its associated migratory pathways, reproductive sites, and associated wetland complex or wetland community system.\n\nSource. #12805, eff 12-15-19; ss by #12954, eff 12-24-19; amd by #13124, eff 10-23-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html"
}
